DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("5/(((x)^(1/2)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin((((e^(x)))^2))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(4, 9) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-1, 9})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-1, 9})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(4, 9) U {-1, 9} U (4, 9) U (4, 9) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((4, 9)) U (4, 9) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-1, 9}))))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-6, -5, -1, 6, 7, 9} - {-8, -6, -2, -1, 4})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-9, -8, -4, -1, 0} U ({-8, -6, -2, -1, 4})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`13*19+2*0`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(247.),width=>7}
---

What is the value of [`5+16+2-8*5`]? [_____]{Formula('-17')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -6, -2, -1, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, -5, -1, 6, 7, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{-9, -8, -4, -1, 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`C \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 < x < 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-1, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cap (B) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A \cup B \cup A \cup A \cap ((A) \cup A \cap (B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 5, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, -2, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, -2, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<4, -2, 3>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, 5, 2>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, -2, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, -2, 3>") x Compute("<10, 5, 2>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -2, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 5, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 5, -10>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, 5, -10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, -2, 8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -2, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -2, 8>") . Compute("<-4, 5, -10>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(0) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>0)}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
